{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The provision fixes effectiveness on \"the first date that all the parties have signed the signature page\" yet also declares the offer and Agreement \"void\" unless employment commences by the April 16, 2012 start date, leaving unclear which event controls if signature and commencement do not align. \"Successful completion of all required pre-employment screenings\" is likewise left to be judged by no stated standard.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"You are expected to complete satisfactorily all assignments and training obligations\" states an expectation rather than a covenant, so whether it imposes an enforceable duty is open. \"Satisfactorily\" is measured only by Wells Fargo Advisors' \"sole discretion\" language applied to the materials, not to performance.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"At least initially, you will be eligible for overtime pay\" fixes no period and no event ending eligibility, so the duration of the overtime entitlement is indeterminate on the face of the clause. The phrase also leaves open whether eligibility is a contractual promise or merely a description of current classification.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Overtime eligibility is made to end \"[o]nce your title changes,\" while Paragraph 3 grants overtime eligibility \"at least initially\" — the two do not say whether the cut-off is the title change, graduation, or attainment of the Series 7, Series 66 and state insurance licenses. The trigger is stated in Paragraph 4 as a compound of four conditions with no statement of what happens if some but not all are met.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"May lead to consequences, up to and including termination from the Training Program\" names no determinate consequence and no standard for choosing among them. \"Failure to behave professionally\" is likewise undefined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The closing sentence preserves all \"Wells Fargo human resources policies and programs\" and \"compliance or regulatory guidelines\" as binding on the employee, which cannot be squared with Paragraph 20's statement that this Agreement \"constitutes the entire understanding\" and Paragraph 8's requirement that changes be signed by a Regional President. A court would have to decide whether unwritten policies form part of the parties' bargain.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The at-will promise that Wells Fargo Advisors \"may terminate the employment of any employee at its discretion at any time for any reason\" sits against Paragraph 10(a), which makes the employee repay Training Costs if \"terminated for any reason at any time,\" and Paragraph 10(b)(i), which conditions forgiveness on five years of continuous employment the employer can unilaterally prevent. Whether the repayment obligation survives an employer-initiated discharge is the construction question.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.32}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"This Agreement serves only as a synopsis of the compensation and other arrangements\" cannot be squared with Paragraph 20's entire-agreement clause or with the substantive covenants in Paragraphs 10, 11 and 12; a synopsis of other arrangements and an integrated contract are different instruments. A court would have to decide whether the operative obligations are these words or the plans and policies they purport to summarize.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.36}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The proviso exempting \"changes to any Wells Fargo Advisors compensation or benefit plans or policies\" from the signed-writing requirement leaves open whether the employer may, by amending a plan, alter terms stated in the Agreement itself — such as the overtime eligibility in Paragraph 3 or the compensation mechanics in Paragraph 9. The exception's boundary against the rule it qualifies is not drawn.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Wells Fargo Advisors shall be liable to you only for compensation earned and received by Wells Fargo Advisors\" makes the firm's receipt, not the employee's performance, the measure of what is owed, and \"any deficit balances (unrelated to the offset of the draw)\" is nowhere defined. What counts as revenue \"fronted\" or \"advanced\" and recoverable in the month of termination is left to be construed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The paragraph uses two different cut-offs — employment \"on the date such payments are received by Wells Fargo Advisors\" and employment \"on the applicable payout date\" — without saying which governs eligibility for the same monthly compensation. Neither \"payout date\" nor the receipt date is defined in the Agreement.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.25}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The dollar amounts of the Training Costs the employee promises to repay are illegible/blank in subparagraphs (i) and (ii), so the essential quantum of the obligation is not stated in the instrument. A court would have to determine the amount, if any, from outside the document.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.40},
    {"issue": "The flat duty to repay when \"terminated for any reason at any time\" is expressly subject to Paragraph 10(b), whose exception (ii)(A) turns on conduct during the year AFTER termination, so the obligation cannot be fixed at termination as 10(a) states. Whether repayment is due immediately or only after the one-year look-forward has run is the conflict.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Forgiveness here requires five continuous years measured from the later of graduation and full registration, while Paragraph 10(c) amortizes the same Training Costs to zero forty-eight months after the start of the second year of employment as a New FA. The two run from different dates and can produce different outcomes for the same termination.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": [
